Lucciola: write the menus' current entry in the secondary colour

The session, scheme and user menus write the entry already chosen in the
palette's primary colour, on the menu's surface_variant. Lucciola's login
palette sets primary to the background colour (so that no focus border,
button fill or avatar ring shows), and the chosen session, the one listed
first after a login with another session, came out black on black. The
current entry takes secondary instead (and the user menu's tint behind it),
which stays readable with any palette that gives secondary a colour of its
own; the entry under the pointer keeps its colours.

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.7.1 tag,
after 0008.

diff --git a/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp b/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
